<speak>
<s>From <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news, this is your briefing for <say-as interpret-as="date" format="dmy">08042026</say-as>.</s>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="95%">
<s>Twenty-eight days of war between the United States and Iran ended — and didn't end — in a single chaotic evening.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Trump announced a ceasefire at half past six Washington time, but within hours Iran launched ballistic missiles at Israel and four Gulf states while Israel's air force continued striking Iranian targets with Washington's explicit blessing.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>This ceasefire is bilateral between Washington and Tehran — Israel isn't party to it, and the nuclear question remains entirely unresolved.</s>
</prosody>
<p>
<s>In politics.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Pakistan's prime minister asked Trump for two more weeks to broker a lasting pause, while simultaneously condemning Iran's missile strikes on Saudi Arabia under a twenty twenty-five bilateral defence pact that treats any such attack as an attack on Pakistan itself.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The contradiction is existential — Islamabad shares a western border with Tehran and has nine million workers across the Gulf.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Sharif's government is now mediator and adversary at once, a position no country can hold for long.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Beijing vetoed Bahrain's UN Security Council resolution to reopen the <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="streɪt əv hɔrˈmuːz">Strait of Hormuz</phoneme> on Tuesday, calling it a pretext for further US-Israeli force — then brokered the ceasefire through Pakistan, Turkey, and Egypt within twenty-four hours.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The pivot from obstruction to mediation mirrors China's twenty twenty-three Saudi-Iran deal.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Whether Beijing claims credit before Trump's May visit to Xi will define who owns this fragile pause.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>An Israeli-backed militia crossed from occupied eastern Gaza into Maghazi refugee camp, clashing with Hamas fighters while Israeli jets struck simultaneously — ten people were killed, including a Hamas unit commander.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Wounded lay in the streets for two hours with no medical access as Israeli forces gave no acknowledgment of the coordinated operation.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>This is proxy warfare inside Gaza — not just occupation, but the deliberate manufacturing of armed factions within the territory.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>South Africa's Social Development Minister Sisisi Tolashe charged her department's Director-General without presidential authority — a move Ramaphosa confirmed she had no legal power to make.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Criminal charges have been filed after two Chinese-gifted SUVs were traced to Tolashe's adult children.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The episode reveals how South Africa's coalition government has become a stage for ministers to entrench patronage networks against presidential oversight.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Nigeria blocked former Senegalese president Macky Sall as Africa's candidate for UN Secretary-General, arguing he bypassed African Union vetting and was forced through a twenty-four-hour silence procedure.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Twenty of fifty-five AU member states filed formal objections.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Without continental endorsement, Sall enters April's selection dialogues weaker than Latin American nominees who carry their regional blocs' full backing.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>A new investigation by The Sentry traced three hundred million dollars looted from Libya's central bank reserves to fund Khalifa Haftar's war machine.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Reserves were pledged at a UAE bank, then loaned to front companies for Wagner Group payments and arms shipments to Sudan — a network spanning Benghazi, Dubai, and Toronto.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Neither the banker who built the pipeline nor Libya's central bank governor has faced charges.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>On the economy.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>The <sub alias="International Energy Agency">IEA</sub> says the Iran war has now surpassed every energy crisis in modern history — crude hit a hundred and fifty dollars a barrel, with eleven million barrels of oil and a hundred and forty billion cubic metres of gas lost daily.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The disruption exceeds the nineteen seventy-three embargo, the nineteen seventy-nine revolution, and the twenty twenty-two shock combined.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Developing nations face the worst food-price spiral in decades, with the <sub alias="International Monetary Fund">IMF</sub> and World Bank convening Monday to coordinate a response.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Six hundred million dollars in crypto short positions were liquidated within minutes of the ceasefire announcement, as Bitcoin surged past seventy-two thousand dollars.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Oil fell sharply from its crisis peaks, reversing weeks of war-driven energy pricing in a single evening.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Whether markets are pricing a genuine resolution or just a two-week pause before the next escalation is the question no trader can answer yet.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Eighteen percent of French filling stations have run dry after TotalEnergies capped unleaded petrol at one euro ninety-nine — below market price — drawing a surge in traffic that exhausted supply.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Paris hasn't said when it'll tap strategic reserves.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Protests are spreading, and France is discovering what Gulf-dependent energy infrastructure feels like when the Gulf is at war.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Binance founder Changpeng Zhao's memoir reveals that Caroline Ellison's public offer to buy <sub alias="F-T-T">FTT</sub> tokens at twenty-two dollars was the fatal mistake that triggered FTX's collapse in twenty twenty-two.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Professional traders immediately shorted through that floor, collapsing the token to five dollars as six billion exited the exchange within seventy-two hours.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>A Signal group connecting Zhao, Sam Bankman-Fried, and rival exchange chiefs during the crisis later drew scrutiny from both the <sub alias="Department of Justice">DOJ</sub> and the <sub alias="Securities and Exchange Commission">SEC</sub>.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In science.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>A Chinese-developed immunotherapy drug called penpulimab has halved the risk of disease progression in nasopharyngeal carcinoma — a cancer linked to the Epstein-Barr virus that's endemic to southern China and Southeast Asia.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The Phase three trial enrolled two hundred and ninety-one patients and showed a fifty-five percent reduction in progression risk when combined with chemotherapy.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>It's a cancer Western pharma has had little incentive to prioritize, and now a drug developed where the disease actually strikes is changing outcomes.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Machine learning models trained on nothing more than age, medications, and existing conditions have achieved a zero point nine one accuracy score for predicting stroke risk in patients with atrial fibrillation — vastly outperforming the standard clinical tool's zero point six seven.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The models identified a hundred and two more high-risk patients per thousand than current guidelines catch.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>External validation held across three separate patient cohorts, but no health system has begun deploying them.</s>
</p>
<p>
<s>In technology.</s><break time="400ms"/>
<s>Germany's domestic intelligence agency and the FBI jointly attributed a campaign that compromised thousands of internet routers to <sub alias="G-R-U">GRU</sub> Unit twenty-six one sixty-five — the Russian military intelligence group known as Fancy Bear.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>At least thirty routers inside Germany required full hardware replacement, not just a software patch.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>While the world watches Iran, Russia's military intelligence hasn't paused its cyber operations across NATO.</s>
<break time="600ms"/>
<s>Bitcoin's <sub alias="elliptic curve digital signature">ECDSA</sub> system could be broken by a quantum computer with roughly four thousand logical qubits — hardware that doesn't exist yet but sits on every major lab's roadmap.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>Mining resists quantum attack for longer, but upgrading Bitcoin's cryptography requires a supermajority vote among miners.</s> <break time="600ms"/> <s>The protocol's upgrade governance is slow by design, and quantum computing won't wait for consensus.</s>
</p>
<break time="1s"/>
<prosody rate="90%">
<s>That's your briefing from <phoneme alphabet="ipa" ph="zʊhd">zuhd</phoneme> news.</s>
</prosody>
</speak>